From 8724cded31dff84796aa0349549372fe2488e7b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:22:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: live island call controls that act, and say what they
 did
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every control in the live island was inert. The Semantic Broker answers an
InvokeAction with a request object and refuses one without a handle token;
the island never sent one, so each press was refused and the refusal was
logged only at debug level. The island now sends a handle token, listens on
the request's Response signal before asking, and logs refusals and failures
as warnings with the broker's reason.

A call now offers deafen beside mute. Luma mutes and deafens at the audio
layer, so the application's own window keeps showing the person as live;
the island is where that state is visible. An engaged microphone or deafen
control is red on a red capsule, the subtitle reads "Muted · 04:12" or
"Deafened · 04:12" in red, and the live dot turns red. The call glyphs are
the shelf's Lucide set: its microphone, and new headphones and
headphones-off glyphs.

In the notification popover the count is the kit's count chip, placed
straight after the "Notifications" title and hidden at zero.
